        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-lancedb): make table initialization atomic",
        "body": "Closes #105680\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe bundled LanceDB memory plugin checked whether the `memories` table existed and then created it in a separate operation. Two OpenClaw processes initializing the same database could both observe the table as absent, race during creation, and fail startup with a missing-table or duplicate-create error.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nKeep the existing fast path for an already-present table, but make the absent-table path use LanceDB's atomic `existOk` create mode. LanceDB 0.30.0 owns the cross-process creation contract, so this avoids adding a separate filesystem lock and keeps schema-row cleanup idempotent.\n\nThe new regression test starts six independent Node processes against one fresh LanceDB directory and requires every process to complete initialization successfully. The same test fails against the previous implementation with a Lance table creation/open race.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGateway and worker processes can initialize the same memory-lancedb store concurrently without intermittent startup failures or index-directory races.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before fix: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-lancedb/memory-lancedb.concurrent.test.ts` fails with a concurrent Lance table initialization error.\n- After fix: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/memory-lancedb/index.test.ts extensions/memory-lancedb/memory-lancedb.concurrent.test.ts` — 126 tests passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_CHECK_CHANGED_REMOTE_CHILD=1 OPENCLAW_CHANGED_LANES_RAW_SYNC=1 CI=1 PNPM_CONFIG_VERIFY_DEPS_BEFORE_RUN=false node scripts/check-changed.mjs -- extensions/memory-lancedb/index.ts extensions/memory-lancedb/memory-lancedb.concurrent.test.ts` — passed.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n\nRemote Testbox delegation was not available locally because the installed Crabbox binary is 0.15.0 while the current Testbox flow requires 0.22.0 or newer; GitHub CI remains the remote verification lane.\n",
